  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\n\ncontext:\n  name: antlrope\n  # antlrope's python floor. Defined here because it is set by the package\n  # itself (the extension is built as abi3/cp312 via nanobind), which is above\n  # conda-forge's global python_min.\n  python_min: \"3.12\"\n  # Pinned to the PUBLISHED release this recipe packages (it builds from the PyPI\n  # sdist below) — not read from the repo's src/antlrope/VERSION, which is\n  # the dev version and may be ahead of the latest release. Placeholder until the\n  # first PyPI release; on conda-forge the autotick bot bumps it per release.\n  version: \"1.0.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  # Prefer the PyPI sdist (carries the vendored runtime). Replace sha256 on each\n  # release.\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/${{ name[0] }}/${{ name }}/antlrope-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: \"a4093fd872516fe3eef3522bc054712194bb7cbd81fd4d647e4d2071893bd648\"\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  # Build via build.sh / build.bat: the unix script forces the Ninja generator\n  # (the linux images export CMAKE_GENERATOR=\"Unix Makefiles\"); the Windows one\n  # keeps the image defaults (its CMAKE_GENERATOR_PLATFORM=x64 conflicts with Ninja).\n  # abi3 / CEP-20: one build (against the 3.12 floor) is installable on any CPython\n  # >=3.12. The extension is compiled with nanobind's STABLE_ABI (pyproject sets\n  # wheel.py-api = \"cp312\"), so it ships as `_native.abi3.so`. `python_version_\n  # independent` makes the package relocate that .so into the target env's\n  # site-packages at install time (it is marked noarch:python but keeps its\n  # platform subdir, since it is still compiled). No per-CPython build matrix.\n  #\n  # entry_points declares the console script so conda generates the launcher at\n  # install time: with a version-independent package, pip's own Windows .exe\n  # launcher bakes the build-prefix python path in as binary data, which prefix\n  # replacement cannot rewrite — the shipped exe fails to start.\n  python:\n    version_independent: true\n    entry_points:\n      - antlrope = antlrope.cli.main:main\n\n# NOTE FOR conda-forge REVIEWERS — why this recipe vendors the ANTLR4 C++ runtime\n# (carried in the sdist under vendor/antlr4-cpp/) instead of depending on the\n# conda-forge `antlr-cpp-runtime` package:\n#   1. We carry two performance patches on the runtime (lock-free DFA-edge reads\n#      and per-DFA write locks; see vendor/antlr4-cpp/UPDATING.md) that are not yet\n#      upstream, so a stock shared runtime would silently drop antlrope's main\n#      speedups. They are proposed upstream as antlr/antlr4#4953 and #4954; once\n#      merged and released the vendored snapshot can be refreshed to stock upstream.\n# The runtime is static-linked (ANTLR4CPP_STATIC, matching the PyPI wheels) and\n# is a few hundred KB compiled in, so vendoring it costs essentially nothing in\n# package size. Once the upstream PRs are merged and released, a future version\n# can drop the patches and consider the shared `antlr-cpp-runtime` package.\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake >=3.21\n    - ninja\n    # Only used when cross-compiling (all platforms currently build natively):\n    # a build-platform python, matching the host python, for pip and\n    # scikit-build-core to run.\n    - if: build_platform != host_platform\n      then:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - cross-python_${{ host_platform }}\n  host:\n    # Build against the 3.12 floor; python-abi3 sets up the Stable-ABI build and\n    # carries the run_exports that pin the runtime to `python >=3.12` + python-abi3.\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - python-abi3 ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - scikit-build-core >=0.10\n    - nanobind >=2.0\n    # Build-time README metadata plugin (in [build-system] requires from 1.0.1;\n    # unused by the 1.0.0 sdist but keeps the autotick version bump working).\n    - hatch-fancy-pypi-readme\n  run:\n    # The host python-abi3 run-exports add the abi3 marker and the\n    # `cpython >=3.12` floor; the plain `python` satisfies the linter.\n    - python\n    - antlr4-python3-runtime >=4.13\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - antlrope\n      pip_check: true\n      # Test at the 3.12 abi3 floor and at the latest python, per the\n      # python-abi3-feedstock example recipe.\n      python_version: [\"${{ python_min }}.*\", \"*\"]\n  - script:\n      - python -c \"import antlrope as a; assert a.__version__\"\n      - antlrope --help\n  # Verify the extension really is Stable-ABI at the declared floor\n  # (from the python-abi3-feedstock example recipe).\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - abi3audit\n    script:\n      - if: unix\n        then: abi3audit $SP_DIR/antlrope/_native.abi3.so -s -v --assume-minimum-abi3 ${{ python_min }}\n        else: abi3audit %SP_DIR%/antlrope/_native.pyd -s -v --assume-minimum-abi3 ${{ python_min }}\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/zuzukin/antlrope\n  repository: https://github.com/zuzukin/antlrope\n  documentation: https://zuzukin.github.io/antlrope/\n  license: Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - vendor/antlr4-cpp/LICENSE.txt\n  summary: >-\n    Fast, C++-accelerated ANTLR runtime for Python: a bulk filtered event-stream\n    facade over the official ANTLR4 C++ runtime, driven by stock Python3-target\n    output.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - analog-cbarber\n",
